ick owner's cadence bit, computed from this tick's own results: true\n    when there are lines to print, when the endpoint reports movement (a\n    woken probe, a published notice), or when either composition still owes a\n-   write.  A pending write keeps cadence at the base interval; it must never\n-   wait out a backoff ceiling.\"\n+   write -- the shell's own or a custody control-plane one.  A pending write\n+   keeps cadence at the base interval; it must never wait out a backoff\n+   ceiling.\"\n   [state server lines]\n   (boolean (or (seq lines)\n                (driver/pending-write? state)\n                (repl.dht/busy? (:repl state))\n+               (custody-owed? state)\n                (and server (serve/moved? server)))))\n \n \n@@ -1024,13 +1095,55 @@\n   \"One shutdown tick for an endpoint that has already been asked to stop.\n    Returns `[server lines stopped?]`.\n \n-   `serve/stopped?` is the whole of the exit condition: an endpoint that never\n-   bound is done on the first tick, because no host exists to report a\n-   `:stopped` fact for it.\"\n+   `serve/stopped?` is the whole of the endpoint's exit condition: an\n+   endpoint that never bound is done on the first tick, because no host\n+   exists to report a `:stopped` fact for it, and an absent endpoint --\n+   a shell run without `--port` -- never had one.\"\n   [server now]\n-  (let [server' (serve/step server now)\n-        [entries server''] (serve/take-outbox server')]\n-    [server'' (mapv entry-text entries) (serve/stopped? server'')]))\n+  (if server\n+    (let [server' (serve/step server now)\n+          [entries server''] (serve/take-outbox server')]\n+      [server'' (mapv entry-text entries) (serve/stopped? server'')])\n+    [server [] true]))\n+\n+\n+(defn shutdown-enter?\n+  \"Whether a shell that just stopped enters the bounded shutdown drain at\n+   all (r3 1.12 as amended by residual 4 and the D15 gate's shutdown row):\n+   there is an endpoint to stop, or the custody comp